.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/logical/join/Join.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":4911,"endPos":4923,"startLine":128,"startLineOffset":16,"endLine":128,"endLineOffset":28,"length":13}],"dstChanges":[{"pos":4898,"endPos":4954,"startLine":121,"startLineOffset":16,"endLine":121,"endLineOffset":72,"length":57}]}]},{"comment":"The old `computeOutput` handled `LEFT`, `RIGHT`, `FULL`, and a default case. The new implementation only supports `LEFT` and throws `UnsupportedOperationException` for everything else. If RIGHT or FULL joins were reachable through any code path (even if rarely used), this is a hard breaking change. Consider whether a deprecation path or a more descriptive error message (naming the unsupported join type) would be safer, e.g.:\n```java\ndefault -\u003e throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\n    \"JOIN type \" + config.type() + \" is not supported in computeOutput; only LEFT is supported\"\n);\n```","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/logical/join/Join.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/logical/join/Join.java-2616:2623,2666:2722,2788:2818,2788:2818,2835:2907,2920:2933,2934:2963,2980:3052,3065:3077,3078:3107,3124:3210,3234:3266,3283:3341-2862:3062,3067:3073,3074:3080,3111:3137,3139:3166,3168:3185,3197:3265,3274:3359,3425:3729,3753:3832","promptId":"#6J2E5","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/logical/join/Join.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/logical/join/Join.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":2616,"endPos":2623,"startLine":76,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":76,"endLineOffset":11,"length":8},{"pos":2666,"endPos":2722,"startLine":77,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":77,"endLineOffset":64,"length":57},{"pos":2788,"endPos":2818,"startLine":79,"startLineOffset":25,"endLine":79,"endLineOffset":55,"length":31},{"pos":2788,"endPos":2818,"startLine":